  "full_text": "I'm Terry Davis, and God said if you made me king, I'd have promised to kill the vile people. So this is my channel, and this song's called Faded Glory. I'm going to put my children on some. We're going to break the United States up into little Catholic kingdoms, put my children on the thrones. And here's the song. The Roman dome is a hoary glory. The melted pilgrims tell a tory story. Faded tongues echo, constellations speckle. Older true blue, better new do. Ruling class crass, union jackass. Faded tongues echo, constellation speckle. Hawking black hole, clocks a craving raven. Spirit quenching, God the mensch is wrenching. Faded tongues echo, constellation speckle. Ode to bear dance, but the crying lion. Hark a babe tattle, now a flowered coward. Faded tongues echo, constellation speckle.",
